menu "STEM_V3 Configuration"

    config STEM_MAX_TORQUE_PERMILLE
        int "Maximum torque limit the console / CLI may set (per-thousand of rated)"
        range 0 3000
        default 500
        help
            Ceiling for the torque limit written to every Eyou actuator's
            Max torque object (0x6072, per-thousand of the rated torque). The
            web console's SET_TORQUE_LIMIT and the CLI's torque_limit refuse a
            value above this, so a browser cannot ask the linkage to push
            harder than the person who flashed it allowed. The drive clamps its
            torque demand to the limit in every mode, so a profile-position
            move cannot exceed it either. 1000 = the rated torque.

    config STEM_BOOT_TORQUE_PERMILLE
        int "Torque limit written at boot (per-thousand of rated)"
        range 0 3000
        default 300
        help
            Written to every motor before the drives are enabled (nothing moves
            harder than this until someone raises the limit from the console
            or the CLI); capped to STEM_MAX_TORQUE_PERMILLE. Found on the
            single-actuator test stand: a torque-limited move is how the
            mechanical limits are found without breaking a linkage.

endmenu
